# ── Bazel ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .bazelrc sets --symlink_prefix=/ so Bazel creates no convenience symlinks at
# all. These patterns are defensive: they keep bazel-bin/bazel-out/etc. and the
# .bazel/ variant out of the index if that setting is ever changed or dropped.
/.bazel/
/bazel-*
# MODULE.bazel.lock is suppressed via `common --lockfile_mode=off` in .bazelrc.
# Ignored as well so re-enabling the lockfile does not silently commit it.
MODULE.bazel.lock

# ── Node / Bun ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The real tree lives in .config/node_modules; /node_modules is the junction
# that makes it reachable (see .tools/automation/bootstrap/link-node-modules).
# Both are generated — only .config/package.json and .config/bun.lock are source.
node_modules/
/node_modules

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cargo's target directory, beside the workspace manifest that produces it.
/.tools/orchestration/bazel/cargo/target/
# labs/gpu-canvas is parked, standalone, and outside that shared workspace —
# its own target directory, from its own `cargo build`.
/labs/gpu-canvas/target/
# Generated FlatBuffers bindings, beside the generator that writes them.
/.tools/generators/out/
# ZigToolchain.ts's auto-downloaded compiler (@carbon/lifecycle) — a cache,
# never committed, same reasoning as Cargo's target/ above.
/.tools/orchestration/toolchains/
dist/
# Per-app build cache the CLI pipeline writes next to a project's dist/.
.carbon-cache/
# zig build's own output — every plugin and the SDK package
# (products/carbon-ext/composition) grows one of each. Bare, not an explicit
# per-path list, because a plugin can exist anywhere a Zig project can.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/
# carbon/bin/<os>/<arch>/ is where every plugin's binary ends up, and the
# ONLY place a vendor one ever lives on disk — InstallPluginUseCase writes a
# fetched plugin straight here, carbon/build.zig never touches it (see its
# own header comment). A local plugin's binary is staged here too, built
# fresh from carbon/plugins/local/<name>/ by carbon/build.zig's subprocess
# orchestration on every `carbon run`/`carbon dev` (SyncPluginsUseCase shells
# it). Entirely build output either way, regenerated on every launch.
# boundaries_test's LOCAL_PLUGIN_ARTIFACT pattern also excludes it, since
# that check does not read .gitignore.
#
# carbon/plugins/vendor/<name>/ holds only that plugin's carbon-plugin.toml
# — small and informational, same posture as carbon/plugins/local/<name>/'s
# own tracked source — so nothing under it needs ignoring.
#
# No leading slash and a `/` in the middle anchors a gitignore pattern to
# THIS file's directory — plain `carbon/bin/**` only ever matched a
# repo-root `carbon/` dir, never `labs/examples/<app>/carbon/`, which is
# where every example app's actually lands. `**/` matches at any depth.
**/carbon/bin/

# EXCEPTION: the launch test's fixture bundle is an INPUT, not build output.
#
# products/carbon/tests/launch.rs starts the real runtime binary against this
# bundle and asserts exit 0, first paint, and the 27 startup phases in order —
# it is the only end-to-end proof the runtime works, and `bazel test //...`
# runs it. Swept up by `dist/` above, it was untracked, so the test had no
# input on a fresh clone even though MIGRATION.md describes it as checked in.
#
# Committed deliberately, and small: a hello-world bundle plus its QuickJS
# bytecode. Regenerate if the bundle format changes, with
#   bazel run //products/carbon-cli:carbon -- build products/carbon/tests/fixtures/hello-app
# the bytecode must match the runtime that reads it.
!/products/carbon/tests/fixtures/hello-app/dist/
!/products/carbon/tests/fixtures/hello-app/dist/**

# ── Stray tool cache from an unexpanded `~` ─────────────────────────────────
# Some cargo/bun invocation on Windows Git Bash left CARGO_HOME (or similar)
# set to the literal two-character string `~` instead of an expanded home
# directory, so the tool wrote its cache as a real directory NAMED `~`
# relative to cwd — observed as products/carbon/~/.cargo/registry/... (500+ MB
# of crates.io cache). `**/` matches at any depth, same reasoning as the
# plugins/*.dll patterns above: this can land wherever a shell happens to
# have cwd'd into when the bad env var was set, not only products/carbon/.
**/~/

# ── Local / machine-specific ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env is machine-specific and the natural place a cache token or signing
# password ends up. .env.example is the committed template — keep them in sync.
.env
.env.local
*.log

# ── OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VS Code's "Local History" extension: timestamped snapshots of every save,
# written outside git entirely. Machine-local, unbounded, and not source.
.history/
# Per-workspace VS Code settings — machine-local (font size, theme, whichever
# extensions happen to be installed), not a project convention to enforce.
.vscode/

# ── Migration scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# labs/e2e holds the throwaway project `carbon init` creates when the CLI loop
# is exercised end to end. Reproducible in one command; not source.
/labs/e2e/

# A carbon app is its own npm project: `carbon build` runs `bun install` in the
# app directory, so every example under labs/ grows a lockfile and a
# node_modules when it is built. The app's package.json is source; what the
# installer resolves from it is not.
/labs/examples/*/bun.lock
